<section class="voice" aria-label="A principal's perspective from Kenya">
  <div class="voice-img" role="img" aria-label="Principal Susan Muthoni Mundia with students and Contentment Foundation staff at OLC Mugoiri Girls School in Kenya" style="background-image:url('/assets/kenya_band.jpg')"></div>
  <div class="voice-panel">
    <div class="voice-inner anim">
      <span class="eyebrow">From a partner school in Kenya</span>
      <img class="qmark" src="/assets/quote_symbol.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
      <blockquote>Teaching is all about a calling, because you have to give so much. You have to support these children emotionally, spiritually, even before academics. They say you only give what you have. And I think this is a skill. And if it can be taught to more young people, it would be a better world.</blockquote>
      <cite><b>Susan Muthoni Mundia</b>Chief Principal, OLC Mugoiri Girls School, Kenya</cite>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
